{"strongs": "H5488", "word": "סוּף", "translit": "suph", "root": "סוה", "morph": "N:N--L", "pos": "noun masculine", "gloss": "reeds, rushes", "definition": "I. סוּף noun masculine Jonah 2:6 reeds, rushes (collective) (probably loan-word from Egyptian ‰wfi , reeds , Steind BAS i. 603 Erman ZMG xivi (1892), 122 ; Semitic according to WMM As. u.Eur.101 ); — 1. rushes , in Nile Exod 2:3 ; Exod 2:5 ( E ); קָנֶה וָסוּף Isa 19:6 (of Egypt). 2. usually in combination יַםסֿוּף probably = sea of rushes or reeds ( > sea of (city) Suph ), which Greek included in wider name θάλασσα Ἐρυθρἀ , Red Sea (compare Di Exod 13:18 and especially WMM As.u.Eur.42f. , who explains as name originally given to upper end of Gulf of Suez, extending into Bitter Lakes, shallow and marshy, whence reeds (probably also reddish colour)); ** compare also Che EB RED SEA . — name applied only to arms of Red Sea; most often \\ \\ a. to Gulf of Suez Exod 10:19 ; Josh 2:10 (both J ), Exod 13:18 ; Exod 15:4 ; Exod 15:22 ; Exod 23:31 (all E ), Deut 11:4 ; Josh 4:23 ( D ), Num 33:10 ; Num 33:11 ( P ), elsewhere late Neh 9:9 ; Ps 106:7 ; Ps 106:9 ; Ps 106:22 ; Ps 136:13 ; Ps 136:15 . \\ \\ b. sometimes to Gulf of Akaba 1Kgs 9:26 , and דֶּרֶךְ יַםסֿוּף Num 21:4 ( E ), probably also Num 14:25 ( E ), Deut 1:40 ; Deut 2:1 perhaps Judg 11:16 ; Jer 49:21 possibly read מִיַּםסֿוּף for ׳ מוֺל ס Deut 1:1 (see infor.).", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB5541')\">BDB5541</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H5488')\">H5488</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB5540')\">BDB5540</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB5542')\">BDB5542</entry></div><p> I. <bdbheb>סוּף</bdbheb> <b>noun masculine</b><sup><ref ref=\"Jonah 2:6\" b=\"32\" cBegin=\"2\" vBegin=\"6\" cEnd=\"2\" vEnd=\"6\" onclick=\"bcv(32,2,6)\">Jonah 2:6</ref></sup> <highlightword>reeds, rushes</highlightword> (collective) (probably loan-word from Egyptian <transliteration><highlight>‰wfi</highlight></transliteration>, <highlight>reeds</highlight>, <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Steind')\">Steind<sup>BAS i. 603</sup></lookup> Erman<sup>ZMG xivi (1892), 122</sup>; Semitic according to <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('WMM')\">WMM<sup>As. u.Eur.101</sup></lookup>); — <div class=\"point\"><b>1.</b> <highlight>rushes</highlight>, in Nile <ref ref=\"Exod 2:3\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"2\" vBegin=\"3\" cEnd=\"2\" vEnd=\"3\" onclick=\"bcv(2,2,3)\">Exod 2:3</ref>; <ref ref=\"Exod 2:5\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"2\" vBegin=\"5\" cEnd=\"2\" vEnd=\"5\" onclick=\"bcv(2,2,5)\">Exod 2:5</ref> (<lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('E')\"><reflink>E</reflink></lookup>); <bdbheb>קָנֶה וָסוּף</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Isa 19:6\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"19\" vBegin=\"6\" cEnd=\"19\" vEnd=\"6\" onclick=\"bcv(23,19,6)\">Isa 19:6</ref> (of Egypt). </div><div class=\"point\"><b>2.</b> usually in combination <bdbheb>יַםסֿוּף</bdbheb> probably = <highlight>sea of rushes or reeds</highlight> ( &gt; <highlight>sea of</highlight> (city) <highlight>Suph</highlight>), which Greek included in wider name <grk>θάλασσα Ἐρυθρἀ</grk>, <highlightword>Red Sea</highlightword> (compare <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Di')\">Di<sup><ref ref=\"Exod 13:18\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"13\" vBegin=\"18\" cEnd=\"13\" vEnd=\"18\" onclick=\"bcv(2,13,18)\">Exod 13:18</ref> and</sup></lookup> especially <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('WMM')\">WMM<sup>As.u.Eur.42f.</sup></lookup>, who explains as name originally given to upper end of Gulf of Suez, extending into Bitter Lakes, shallow and marshy, whence <highlight>reeds</highlight> (probably also reddish colour)); </div><div class=\"remarks\"><b>**</b>compare also Che<sup>EB RED SEA</sup>. — name applied only to arms of Red Sea; most often <br>\\&emsp;\\&emsp;<b>a.</b> to <highlight>Gulf of Suez</highlight> <ref ref=\"Exod 10:19\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"10\" vBegin=\"19\" cEnd=\"10\" vEnd=\"19\" onclick=\"bcv(2,10,19)\">Exod 10:19</ref>; <ref ref=\"Josh 2:10\" b=\"6\" cBegin=\"2\" vBegin=\"10\" cEnd=\"2\" vEnd=\"10\" onclick=\"bcv(6,2,10)\">Josh 2:10</ref> (both <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('J')\"><reflink>J</reflink></lookup>), <ref ref=\"Exod 13:18\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"13\" vBegin=\"18\" cEnd=\"13\" vEnd=\"18\" onclick=\"bcv(2,13,18)\">Exod 13:18</ref>; <ref ref=\"Exod 15:4\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"15\" vBegin=\"4\" cEnd=\"15\" vEnd=\"4\" onclick=\"bcv(2,15,4)\">Exod 15:4</ref>; <ref ref=\"Exod 15:22\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"15\" vBegin=\"22\" cEnd=\"15\" vEnd=\"22\" onclick=\"bcv(2,15,22)\">Exod 15:22</ref>; <ref ref=\"Exod 23:31\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"23\" vBegin=\"31\" cEnd=\"23\" vEnd=\"31\" onclick=\"bcv(2,23,31)\">Exod 23:31</ref> (all <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('E')\"><reflink>E</reflink></lookup>), <ref ref=\"Deut 11:4\" b=\"5\" cBegin=\"11\" vBegin=\"4\" cEnd=\"11\" vEnd=\"4\" onclick=\"bcv(5,11,4)\">Deut 11:4</ref>; <ref ref=\"Josh 4:23\" b=\"6\" cBegin=\"4\" vBegin=\"23\" cEnd=\"4\" vEnd=\"23\" onclick=\"bcv(6,4,23)\">Josh 4:23</ref> (<lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('D')\"><reflink>D</reflink></lookup>), <ref ref=\"Num 33:10\" b=\"4\" cBegin=\"33\" vBegin=\"10\" cEnd=\"33\" vEnd=\"10\" onclick=\"bcv(4,33,10)\">Num 33:10</ref>; <ref ref=\"Num 33:11\" b=\"4\" cBegin=\"33\" vBegin=\"11\" cEnd=\"33\" vEnd=\"11\" onclick=\"bcv(4,33,11)\">Num 33:11</ref> (<lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('P')\"><reflink>P</reflink></lookup>), elsewhere late <ref ref=\"Neh 9:9\" b=\"16\" cBegin=\"9\" vBegin=\"9\" cEnd=\"9\" vEnd=\"9\" onclick=\"bcv(16,9,9)\">Neh 9:9</ref>; <ref ref=\"Ps 106:7\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"106\" vBegin=\"7\" cEnd=\"106\" vEnd=\"7\" onclick=\"bcv(19,106,7)\">Ps 106:7</ref>; <ref ref=\"Ps 106:9\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"106\" vBegin=\"9\" cEnd=\"106\" vEnd=\"9\" onclick=\"bcv(19,106,9)\">Ps 106:9</ref>; <ref ref=\"Ps 106:22\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"106\" vBegin=\"22\" cEnd=\"106\" vEnd=\"22\" onclick=\"bcv(19,106,22)\">Ps 106:22</ref>; <ref ref=\"Ps 136:13\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"136\" vBegin=\"13\" cEnd=\"136\" vEnd=\"13\" onclick=\"bcv(19,136,13)\">Ps 136:13</ref>; <ref ref=\"Ps 136:15\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"136\" vBegin=\"15\" cEnd=\"136\" vEnd=\"15\" onclic